# A feature with an open task resumes coding at the first open task and redoes no finished task.
id: codify-open-task
skill: highway-codify
fixture: codify-open-task
open: /highway-codify Restock Alerts
ask: Where would you like to go next?
say: [decline] Nothing else.
writes: code/**
expect: contains code/restock-alerts/.highway/features/002-check-reorder-points/codify-tasks.md :: [X] T002
expect: contains code/restock-alerts/.highway/features/002-check-reorder-points/codify-tasks.md :: [X] T003
expect: contains code/restock-alerts/.github/workflows/reorder-check.yml :: upload-artifact
expect: heading code/restock-alerts/README.md :: ## User Guide
covers: 2c0b10922a8f A task that cannot be finished stops the run with that task and every later task open. The next run starts at the first open task, redoes no finished task, and runs no check.
covers: bf767f40cbdb Coding starts with no question after the task list is written. Every standard a task names, and each existing file it names, is read before its files are written, and no other automation file is read, the earlier one winning a disagreement, and each task is marked `[X]` before the next begins.
reaches: code
reaches: close
